  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: native binaries move to Google's official LiteRT-LM v0.16.0 C API prebuilts (one monolithic library per platform: linux-x64 now needs the system Vulkan loader (libvulkan1), win-x64 no longer needs the VC++ Redistributable, Android keeps GPU sampling with the embedded sampler, iOS ships the official CLiteRTLM.xcframework). Constrained decoding works on linux-x64 (guard removed); text LoRA is applied on LoRA-enabled bundles; new EnableYnnpack engine option; NoRepeatNgramSize / SuppressTokens on the MEAI and Semantic Kernel options. Also carries the v0.15.0 cycle: per-send decoding controls (penalties, no-repeat-ngram, suppress tokens, thinking budget, regex/JSON-schema constraints), the LlGuidance constraint provider, the KV overflow guard recalibrated to the new prefill planning, and Clone() now requiring an advanced conversation. The managed assembly requires the same-version runtime packages (LiteRT-LM v0.16.0). Full notes: https://github.com/OrihuelaConde/LiteRtLmSharp/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
